*Liability:*  Liability clause excludes indirect and consequential losses for Fortem and not Bolt. This leaves Bolt exposed to a broader range of liabilities. If something goes wrong, Bolt  might not be able to claim for indirect or consequential losses they suffer, even if those losses are significant. Bolt’s liability under the agreement is not limited. 

I advise a limit on Bolt’s liability shall be included in the Terms and conditions and Bolt’s liability for indirect losses shall be excluded as mentioned above. 

{color:#ff5630}+It's my preference not to change this agreement because it's a standard boiler plate contract for a 3m x 3m stand at an expo. I am comfortable with us assuming the associated risk/liability (in conjunction with the 100s of other exhibitors for our activities at this event who would be signing this same agreement).+{color}

