Hi Tatsiana,

Please find the answers to your questions below:

{quote}# We would need to know *all the data the team wants to collect for this purpose of ‘analyse general behaviour, to figure out what we should build’.* We cannot approve all data to be collected unless we know all of them are really necessary.
## Can you please ask them to assess how all data is necessary for their purposes under the following model:
### {{Data category}} - {{necessary}} / {{good to have}} / {{can skip}}
### Example, ‘card number’ - can skip
## We can agree on collecting only necessary data and skip all other data from the start{quote}

You can consider every field under the “Unmasked” heading [here|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rQglUm4NYcPlFR3dHJEnouoQ8-Zwaa1SlsTUSR-BLFM/edit#heading=h.momk4lizcrf3] as necessary for us to track.

{quote}# Can you also advise *where this data would be kept:* would it be linked to the user’s profile in Admin or would we keep it in a separate DB with a user ID link?{quote}

Internal analytics data warehouse, joinable with user_id link. Not stored in admin

{quote}# How long *would you keep this data in our systems*? Can you please also *clarify why would you keep it within this period?*{quote}

We do not have a fixed time limit for this, though we can consider such. Data will be retained to understand long-term user behaviour, how it changes over time and make correlations over time. It is very valuable to understand how user behaviour changes from their first signup over time, so there are reasons to retain this data over the user’s lifetime.

{quote}# Users have the right to request the deletion of this data from our systems. If it’s requested, would you be able to delete it? If no, why?{quote}

It would be a manual process, but I suppose that it is possible.

{quote}# You said that the team needs to _‘_*_to get better data_* _we do need to make as much data visible as possible’._ Can you clarify what you mean *_by better data_* and why current set-up does not work for the team?
## I would appreciate detailed answer here as we have to document the real need of changing the approach{quote}

At the moment, we do not have a granular understanding of how users engage with different screens. Having video replays would give us a deep understanding of the pain points users face and how they engage with different content in the app. This will help us identify areas of improvement and new opportunities. This information will be very valuable to our designers so they can gain an understanding of how users engage with the platform, and provide qualitative insights to complement the quantitative data we collect.

{quote}# Do we need to *collect user ID, name, and other data that can identify the user in our systems? a. Can we anonymise user clicks, so that no direct identifiers like name, email, phone, ID, card number, etc is not collected?*{quote}

We will need to collect user_id to join back with internal data to develop a richer understanding of the user, for example, by understanding their final orders, order history and other characteristics.

{quote}# Would the team *use any AI models for analysing general behaviour and figuring out what we should build?*{quote}

We are unlikely to use these insights in our AI models, at least in the foreseeable future.

{quote}# Would we *collect it in all countries?*{quote}

Yes

{quote}# Would it include *only web users? How many web users we have in a month please?*{quote}

Only web users. currently we have 23,000+ in July and growing every month

