# {color:#4c9aff}*This specific ticket:*{color} 
## *We agreed to approach this case (due to the tight deadline and unknown new process of getting fleet’s approval) based on the reason the fleet cannot approve the driver’s deletion*:
### If this is due to any debts, fines, damages *owned to Bolt*, we would {color:#bf2600}advise the driver that they need to pay off these ones and we would be able to delete the account.{color}
### If this is *due to any reasons btw the driver and the fleet*, we would contact the fleet explaining that we have to satisfy the request under the privacy law and we do not have any legitimate reason to reject this,{color:#bf2600} and advise that they should solve their matters outside of Bolt.{color}
### If this is *due to an unknown reason,* we would contact the fleet advising the above and delete the driver’s account following our documented guidelines for such cases.
# {color:#4c9aff}*The process itself:*{color}
## Gab and I agreed that we would need to *consider the role of the fleets as the drivers' employers in this cases.* Fleets onboard drivers and it makes sense for them to control when the driver wants to be deleted from the platform
### For sure, *the fleet would be entitled to take a lead only in relation to the account creation/deletion and changing account details that can affect the fleet itself.* Other matters like consent to marketing, objection to Bolt’s data processing, etc that do not affect the fleet, should not go under the fleet’s responsibility.
## The ticket for discussing this process is created for the *CS Knowledge Management Team (*[+*CCM-17820*+|https://taxify.atlassian.net/servicedesk/customer/portal/4/CCM-17820]*)* and [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LSS/queues/issue/LSS-38537] and [here|https://taxify.atlassian.net/jira/servicedesk/projects/LSS/queues/issue/LSS-38534] for the Privacy legal team.

