Hi, [~accountid:61debf39e67ea2006b3a1cb5]! 

Yes, you can implement e-receipts.

Please keep in mind that e-receipts can be issued under following conditions:

* obtaining consent of the purchaser;
* sending the e-receipt in a manner agreed with the purchaser - e-receipts can be delivered via SMS, e-mail or a mobile application;
* conducting the process in a way which does not require the purchaser to provide personal information.



The expression of consent most often takes the form of:

* accepting the T&Cs including consent for receiving e-receipts
* statements at the time of purchase: for example, a checkbox next to the statement of consent to receive an e-receipt;

