Hi all,

I’ve been exploring the options internally:

* Product - not improvements anticipated for bolt send until 2025
* Physical form - possible but may cause problems for us down the line in terms of traceability - it’s also not a very good user experience



What I would like to propose is the following. After talking to the business team, it looks like they can set up business accounts in a way that any client that wishes to use the service has to input an expense note. So in collaboration with the business team, they’ll onboard clients to be able to use this service one by one with proper training. What they will be instructing clients to do is the following:

* Input all the required details in the expense note so that the business can keep a copy
* Once the order is placed, require the business to input the exact same text in app chat so that the driver/courier also has a copy

The will be asked to submit the following details:

* A description of all the goods being transported;
* The value of the goods;
* The unit quantity;
* The date of the delivery;
* The destination address;
* The name and address and VAT number of the supplier and;
* The name and address and VAT number of the person to whom the supply is made (optional)



What I need from you is:

* [~accountid:610279973900e60070a3495c] the list above is extensive as it gets. It’s what DfK had shared with us when we requested their input - in your view will having the text in the app be enough? I personally think it’s superior to a piece of paper. Like this we can also make sure the business team do spot checks on these trips and can check via admin if they are following the correct protocol
